    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0727" n="625" xml:id="pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/769: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-08T18:00:00+01:00">August 8, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 8—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>455. My 488, August 6, 6 p.m., paragraph 2.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d505-f1"/> I
                    understand from British sources that the conference between the representatives
                    of France, Great Britain and Italy will take place on August 15th presumably at
                    Paris and that as the conversations are to take place in France an invitation
                    will be sent by Laval to the Italian Government to send a representative. It is
                    stated that Laval and Eden will represent their respective Governments and that
                    presumably the Italians will send Aloisi.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
